            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "This sentence and the next one are confusing. I don't quite understand them. Can you rewrite them to make them clearer?\n\nAlso, the method name is incorrect if it is referring to the ChassisStatusMonitor class. The method is getPowerGood().\n\nIn general, commit messages should describe the end result of applying the commit rather than the internal details. You normally don't need to discuss new methods or data members. That is clear from the file diffs. The commit message is explaining the high level \"what/why\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brendan Singer",
                        "email": "brendansinger2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "brendansinger2-cyber"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-chassis-power/src/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 54,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "The method signature and std::move() is confusing.\n\nYou want to share the pointer, so wouldn't you want to pass the shared pointer as a reference, and then just do a normal assignment without the std::move()?\n\n```\nvoid Chassis::setSystemStatusMonitor(\n    std::shared_ptr<ChassisStatusMonitor>& monitor)\n{\n    systemMonitor = monitor;\n```\n\nRight now you are creating a copy, and then moving the internals of the copy to your data member. Maybe that is the same thing? Seems confusing though.\n\nSee https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/memory/shared_ptr/operator%3D"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-chassis-power/src/chassis.cpp",
                    "line": 54,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brendan Singer",
                        "email": "brendansinger2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "brendansinger2-cyber"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-chassis-power/src/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
                        "email": "shawnmm@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "smccarney"
                    },
                    "message": "As noted on line 162, this is a system status monitor rather than a chassis level monitor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-chassis-power/src/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Brendan Singer",
                        "email": "brendansinger2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "brendansinger2-cyber"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "phosphor-chassis-power/src/chassis.hpp",
                    "line": 184,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Shawn McCarney",
